Minetka, her Demigodess chaotic elven Wizard, ascended! I'm so
impressed with her achievement, that i barely can breathe. Here is her
story.

But first some background. I started playing Nethack some 8 years ago.
Thanks to Duncan Booth excellent port of this game to Psion 5 i could
play it on the go. 3 or 4 years ago my Psion finally died, and for
some time i gave up. 2 years ago, however, i bought a laptop, and
started playing more and more often, concentrating on Wizards. But
never got even to Medusa.

Countless YASD later i had a character which was looking promising.
With early wish (SDSM), good staff collected early (BoS, BoH, magic
marker) and some powerful spells it was quite probable, that she will
get really deep. When we left for our two weeks long holidays im
Croatia i had a feeling, that this time she will ascend, my family
like it or not :-)

But it wasn't Minetka. It was a different wizard named Rekrutacja,
which had so many staff to move around, that playing her was not
really that fun.

So, i started romance with Minetka. This wasn't intended to be a
serious game. With a name like that (you can easily guess what that
means in polish...), she was meant to just give me some fun and space
for experiments. However, as our holidays progressed, she was more and
more powerful. And by the time Rekrutacja finally died (horrible
spelling accident -  you should always check how to write word
"Croesus") she was, well, quite an attractive woman.

Early game was pretty predictable, with "sleep" spell and pets as an
important survival tactic. Sokoban gave her reflection and i must say,
that lack of BoH was a problem. Finally i had to wish for one from
Castle wand (the only WoW in the game). The only stash was in Gnomish
Town, which housed coaligned altar.

With ring of polymorph control she turned into silver dragon on the
first polymorph trap and gave birth to some important pets, which
helped her to survive.

There were only one really scary accident during her travel. On Medusa
Island electric eel destroyed her rings of levitation, teleport
control and polymorph control. Trapped on the island she had no choice
than dig down - but below was only Castle and an master mind flier,
which made her forget most of she learned.

So she found herself trapped beetween the water and water, without any
means to go back to her stash (and as she had no BoH, so her supplies
were very limited). However, RNG quickly send her a soldier with a
bugle, and Castle wand of wishing helped her to get back on the right
track with spellbook of identify as a high priority. This event
tempted her to genocide all h (and some lichs).

One wish was wasted on Staff of Aesculapius, which blasted her several
times...

After that game was much easier than expected. Polypiling gave her
almost nothing, but few nurses met in the meantime boosted her HP over
150. Donations and scrolls (plenty of those) lowered her AC to -20. By
this time she learned how to charm monsters, which was her main
strategy for Gehennom.

And Gehennom was much easier than expected. Vlad was killed by her
pets (namely an Archon, which died soon after that), Wizard double
troubled at the very beginning, and was really hard to kill, but
finally gave up.  After that she simply zapping him with one of her
WoD.

Another scary moment was on the planes, when she realized that she has
no means of portal detection with her. She managed however to find all
portals with heavy use of conflict.

And this is another lesson to remember - using conflict when getting
to Astral is not good, and wishing for blessed figurine of an Archon
with conflict still on your fingers is a bad idea. That wasted her
last wish, Famine stole her last charge on wand of death, and she
faced serious problems. Even with 3 AoLS and some scrolls of charging
she wouldn't probably get to third altar, but... the very first was
aligned.

minetka, chaotic female elven Wizard






